WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.467
Hi, my name is Nikema Prophet.

00:02.467 --> 00:05.500
I'm a software engineer and developer advocate,

00:05.500 --> 00:10.300
and I want to tell you how Twilio influenced my tech career.

00:10.533 --> 00:14.400
My first tech conference was SIGNAL in 2019,

00:14.400 --> 00:17.633
and I attended as a scholarship recipient.

00:17.633 --> 00:21.067
And it was at the event that happened before the conference

00:21.067 --> 00:23.167
for the scholarship recipients

00:23.167 --> 00:26.767
where I discovered that developer relations

00:26.767 --> 00:29.433
and community roles existed.

00:29.433 --> 00:33.400
And I knew immediately that this is what I wanted to do

00:33.400 --> 00:34.767
in my tech career.

00:34.867 --> 00:39.767
I walked away from SIGNAL with a Magic Leap,

00:39.767 --> 00:43.833
which was super cool, that I won during TwilioQuest,

00:43.833 --> 00:47.233
and also feeling like I had a place in tech

00:47.233 --> 00:48.800
and I belonged in tech.

00:48.800 --> 00:51.733
And it was a really positive experience.

00:51.833 --> 00:56.533
I applied for the software engineering apprenticeship.

00:56.533 --> 00:59.867
Unfortunately, I didn't make it past the coding screen,

00:59.867 --> 01:01.533
but I was still...

01:01.533 --> 01:05.233
I still felt really positive about Twilio as a company

01:05.233 --> 01:09.133
just because of the people who I met that were working there.

01:09.133 --> 01:13.233
Like, everyone was very welcoming and inclusive

01:13.233 --> 01:16.300
and were just really supportive

01:16.300 --> 01:19.300
of someone who was trying to break into tech.

01:19.400 --> 01:22.833
Fast forward to 2026,

01:22.833 --> 01:27.100
and I participated in CodeTV's Web Dev Challenge.

01:28.700 --> 01:30.633
Twilio was the sponsor,

01:30.633 --> 01:35.833
so it felt very nostalgic to be building with Twilio again.

01:36.333 --> 01:41.067
It brought me back to that TwilioQuest in 2019.

01:41.367 --> 01:45.167
Today I'm applying for the Developer Evangelist role,

01:45.167 --> 01:48.167
and I wanted to show you that I can build with Twilio.

01:48.167 --> 01:52.333
So I added an AI guide to this site

01:52.333 --> 01:56.933
where you can chat by text or by voice with my AI guide

01:56.933 --> 02:01.233
and ask it about my experience.

02:01.333 --> 02:03.733
So I hope that you will check it out.

02:03.733 --> 02:07.633
You can either click the red phone on the game,

02:07.667 --> 02:10.567
or you can just scroll down the page

02:10.567 --> 02:12.567
until you reach the AI guide.

02:12.567 --> 02:14.067
I hope you will check it out,

02:14.067 --> 02:18.367
and I am super excited to continue the conversation.

